{"step_index":7034,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T14:19:15Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T14:19:15Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T14:19:19Z\nThe search for \"\"iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation\" \"DENY\" override edit\" returned the following summary:\nTo manage the **`iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation`** organization policy constraint, you must have the **Organization Policy Administrator** role (`roles/orgpolicy.policyAdmin`) at the organization level[1][2][3].\n\nIf you are blocked by this policy, here is the standard process to override it for a specific project or the entire organization[1][3]:\n\n### 1. Verify Your Permissions\n*   You must be assigned the **Organization Policy Administrator** role at the **organization level**[2][3]. \n*   This role often does not appear in the role list for individual projects; you must select your organization in the resource picker (top-left of the Google Cloud Console) to grant or verify this role[4][2][3].\n\n### 2. Override the Policy\nOnce you have the required permissions, you can modify the policy at the project or organization level[3]:\n1.  Go to the **[Organization Policies](https://console.cloud.google.com/iam-admin/orgpolicies)** page in the Google Cloud Console[5][3].\n2.  Use the filter to search for **`iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation`**[1][3].\n3.  Click on the policy name to open its details[1][3].\n4.  Click **Manage policy**[1][3].\n5.  Select **Override parent's policy** (this is critical if the policy is being inherited from the organization)[6][7][3].\n6.  Under **Enforcement**, select **Off** (or \"Not enforced\")[8][5][3].\n7.  Click **Set policy**[8][3].\n\n### Important Troubleshooting Notes\n*   **Dual Constraints:** Google Cloud often utilizes both a legacy constraint (`iam.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation`) and a managed constraint (`iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation`)[1][9]. If you disable one but the block persists, ensure you have checked and overridden **both**[1][9].\n*   **Propagation Time:** Changes to organization policies are not always instantaneous and may take a few minutes to propagate across your projects[10].\n*   **Security Recommendation:** Service account keys are long-lived, portable credentials that pose significant security risks[5][11]. Where possible, consider alternatives like **Workload Identity Federation** or service account impersonation to avoid using static keys entirely[5][11].\n\nSources:\n[1] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHCi-QZhmzCGe5zvtBQBMjQdUAldP59xuS9R3AmX7ytTbWEgKUX_CZgxnQw6H9MdhTJaOYg0aLSdZkmtgDFN04ggeGOWJiM6XbO11sIFR3gK6efrjSHZ2yV2oG6uAGD0NoRNgUefSsjF0_vsobEg2iF_rOqBt1vd0GnXzTXO0IlXTM-tH69-lkcxoElkl_idw7oWM7j2AZiBB40Df57)\n[2] [subsplash.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHQ3IcgOv4a0pA-dUW7vSO_MvLEnHHOHPsm7oIaOQ_KzamJXewEDe41ovjOHacmE5ko5Y8gqos-2Idj6qMoLafTjqsWJJ3V6G1psFETqBkNCdhTpzS_bSr7gOeRpAfkYbAX7-DtT-YAjxWjNaDWWBqr34Bs3ANQjBmZb3OHlCT8TXXuY4T-qGlUsR7GEZabCEeKm1yhRg2aqR2kR5HAcsfqdbT-yC50G4odg43p78Lx)\n[3] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFekq6rC8VBDZ8iyng8DzK1rrEaqKUvWcEWaZ6hQjgG5hkw6extWE1gSEklr1VCyEhjzoj4fefq6GTISTYNnBTGEHbyyOz6bJX2lU9AoYH65QGsIKuQYheNZ99ixvqrcfnLcKBvY1KyGDv5ezJIH-7mSWC7-w5d)\n[4] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGZY21Oj2DYH6AwXDJu2LT-XWdHORdro5HBWvQtrB8OywRTmgLNHmsZNRZCqfKnu9RXYAosezo77HREJprkQbdySNtO4r05E8PiqQO8VagziWWDc8vPUCf_JeqBUwyiR4O9GWtr60UUx9D_jWaIj9sfZMzJpJun7ypUks3spqy9bZ81aI4YZxLilaNRzpQYkuqdUs7VSmbrWe8=)\n[5] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGrZawelSUvc5L0peJLl4U72miZfffj5rJ-lBUCktXyvtwLVRgKmtctyq_cBOoBH0LgpF6vonGYdbh68qng7kN6VFGfsQZYzE4qQNCQbOdHKNd9OhnZGBYyCXN-3GGmDTc4NQwpr-mMsNG79z6yEFK__Byyl14MdV5JErNQLiVj0pEYLNKcPSn3ZVlD5B-obVLdWqA=)\n[6] [reddit.com](https://ver