{"step_index":7036,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T14:19:24Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T14:19:24Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T14:19:28Z\nThe search for \"\"iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation\" \"secure by default\" opt out or disable\" returned the following summary:\nThe organization policy `iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation` is part of Google Cloud's **\"secure-by-default\"** baseline, which is automatically enforced for all organizations created on or after May 3, 2024[1][2][3].\n\nThis policy is designed to improve security by preventing the creation of long-lived, user-managed service account keys, which are a common vector for security compromises[4][5][6].\n\n### Can you opt out or disable it?\nYes, you can disable or override this policy, but it requires specific administrative privileges[7][8]. Because it is an organization-level policy, you cannot override it if you only have project-level permissions[9][10].\n\n### How to Disable or Modify the Policy\nTo modify this constraint, you must have the **Organization Policy Administrator** (`roles/orgpolicy.policyAdmin`) or **Organization Administrator** (`roles/resourcemanager.organizationAdmin`) role[7][10][8].\n\n1.  **Navigate to Organization Policies:** Go to the Google Cloud Console, select your organization, and navigate to **IAM & Admin > Organization policies**[10][8].\n2.  **Locate the Constraint:** Search for `iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation`[10][8].\n3.  **Manage/Edit Policy:** Click on the policy name. If it is enforced at the organization level, you can choose to:\n    *   **Disable it:** Change the enforcement state to \"Off\" (or \"Not enforced\")[8].\n    *   **Create an Exception:** Depending on your needs, you may be able to set the policy to apply only to specific projects or folders rather than the entire organization[6][10].\n\n### Important Considerations\n*   **Legacy vs. Managed Constraints:** Google is transitioning from legacy policies (e.g., `iam.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation`) to managed versions (`iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation`)[11][10]. If you are still blocked after modifying one, **check if both the legacy and managed versions are enforced**[10]. You may need to disable both to fully enable key creation[10].\n*   **Security Recommendation:** Google strongly recommends using more secure alternatives to long-lived keys, such as **Workload Identity Federation** or service account impersonation, rather than disabling this policy[7][5][12]. If you must use keys, ensure they are rotated frequently and managed according to security best practices[3][5].\n\nSources:\n[1] [techcolumnist.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH4_Z-zezSmmRQNgMc-M78WK3WN3rTE0ociA6_sKE0GnePb15QezQMO3MYr5vETqtslmWS1giFepUe4r577np4uiDBXS4ZydauAmTWVa8USvkgtWgveCbEZlXbITMlYST_-tMa-6UfKcWHPUCNvy5tSYS4c2wEymJuBhInBGhGnmuEoEBR3Sn72-d7C3hAt1G0WMHKQ_mW7H-8RWGxrIDbr)\n[2] [jayendrapatil.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFUCdWDRzADGQpf7SLtnOtfuVrDNHCL_WRxLAyRp8nloET54YCvRX0Eai06dyzOtSiFqOpalMxWC8llK92WzmFL7q_CGvV859v1eY8FdODka6YDSQjlNkIHWmnvAUEnFuc5B3qO)\n[3] [techcolumnist.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQESO4aFLMM8PGyNeFtuGRNkbA-2uQpCKo0TUumngYF2TguKDpncf5AQziy8iosmkVbZuKHs6bz0UGWGRHWkG5cPyX54gsC7ksRSkgx3c1yfAFULR9qL8puHGrnInJx74Bio6kfaWcOTYz3_OMKVCMPhlSRddOgrcnEL1ouZTciQdFSELR78HV_dpMBgBZzsD9zkmCeuB7yepLUgAze1GQ==)\n[4] [datadoghq.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFlyeUTotr7E-QSYic5uPlZoFP7hq-vKo2-cqxjoiJKsT6p228zb-NfRMXAMHWLzkhgeZPMBYT2Hmv9Fxz9l5jobkegzb4mIB5RzO_En4V4xWlN8p6k0jubhG2tJU6PPU9SkK73rFgmX8DFGKgMnzX7VQTV60ZJi70=)\n[5] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFks8cduBqpo6Ze5fkO-H5xK3HBk_ZeOjdDbIbV_KROwMgRxEEO23UuYEcTGpjpKfz9tXDFK7f60olG-JNNfcPKBjJ4mugQLSEJ0VykKZpYst1GH2Wt1d3